    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a bit of a struggle for me. I never really excelled at it in school, partly because my education stopped early and partly because it just didn't click with me like history or computer science did. My dad had a PhD, so he tried to help, but it often felt overwhelming. Now, as an unemployed person in Milan, I don’t use math much in daily life, but I try to keep an open mind about it.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, sometimes. The abstract concepts and the way they build on each other can feel intimidating. My high neuroticism makes me overthink things, so even simple problems might trigger anxiety. But I’m trying to work through that, especially since my openness is high—I like learning new things, even if it’s tough.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I haven’t used AI for math recently, but I’ve thought about it. With my moderate conscientiousness, I might not stick with it long-term, but tools like chatbots could break things down in a way that feels less scary. My extraversion means I’d probably prefer learning with others, though.",
